          "unit": "nodes",
          "signal": "operation-count",
          "budget": {
            "max": 16384
          },
          "notes": "O(m log n): every move's casts descend the tree. Tree nodes grow with log n but coding-tooling has no logarithmic bound and its linear marginal-rate test is too strict for integer tree depths, so the class is held by a budget: a linear scan or a lost tree would exceed it by orders of magnitude at the largest town."
        },
        {
          "name": "tree-nodes-per-character",
          "unit": "nodes",
          "signal": "operation-count",
          "budget": {
            "max": 128
          },
          "notes": "O(log n) per character; held by budget for the same reason."
        },
        {
          "name": "exact-tests",
          "unit": "tests",
          "signal": "operation-count",
          "budget": {
            "max": 256
          },
          "growth": [
            {
              "dimension": "characters",
              "bound": "linear"
            }
          ],
          "notes": "Neighbour tests: linear in movers at fixed density. With density they grow faster than linear here (more slides per move when crowded), so density is held by a budget far below all-pairs (32 movers would be 1024 tests per cast)."
        }
      ]
